if dengue's a_min is the lowest AND its p05 w / w<1 are the smallest, the multiplicative
score is the fault: it cannot widen a near-zero interval, so ACI pays for those cells by
inflating every other cell in the panel. The fix is an additive floor on the widening, not
a dengue exclusion. If a_min is ordinary and the widths are not extreme, drop this line of
inquiry -- dengue is simply the panel with the most origins (2885) for drift to accumulate.
